# Sites and Sheaves, Chapter 1: Introduction

The source span is entirely introductory prose.  It records the historical
motivation from Grothendieck's study of sheaves in the étale topology, the
terminology distinction from SGA4 (where the book's notion is called a
category endowed with a pretopology), the motivation for working with a
specified class of coverings, and the attribution to ArtinTopologies.  It
also states the scope convention that universes will not be used.  These are
history, terminology, motivation, bibliography, and scope rather than
standalone mathematical declarations; the later source sections introduce
the site definitions that use this terminology.
